Haan bhai. Pehle roadmap lock karte hain, phir us roadmap ke according ek-ek topic ko deeply karenge. Abhi commands nahi—pehle Linux ka complete syllabus + industry/DevOps mapping clear karte hain.

Tumhara target hona chahiye:

Linux user → Linux administrator mindset → Linux troubleshooting → Linux automation → Linux in DevOps → production-ready Linux knowledge

🐧 Linux → DevOps Industry Roadmap
Phase 0 — Linux ki Story & Foundation

Sabse pehle samjhenge Linux aaya kyu.

Topics
Unix kya tha?
Unix ki problems/limitations
GNU Project
Richard Stallman & Free Software
Linux kernel
Linus Torvalds
Linux + GNU = complete Linux distributions
Open Source kya hai?
Linux distributions kya hoti hain?
Ubuntu vs Debian vs RHEL vs CentOS/Rocky/AlmaLinux
Linux ka industry me rise
Linux vs Windows
Linux server ke liye itna popular kyu hai?
DevOps connection

Cloud servers, CI/CD servers, Docker hosts, Kubernetes nodes, web servers—Linux ka huge role.

Phase 1 — Linux Architecture 🧠

Yahan se actual deep Linux start.

Samjhenge:
User
 ↓
Applications
 ↓
Shell
 ↓
System Calls
 ↓
Kernel
 ↓
Hardware
Topics
Kernel
Shell
Terminal
System calls
User space vs Kernel space
Hardware interaction
Linux architecture
Boot process ka overview
BIOS/UEFI
Bootloader / GRUB
Kernel loading
init/systemd
Industry

Production server boot hone se lekar application run hone tak kya hota hai—ye samajh aayega.

